  "summary": "Oakland City Council's Public Safety Committee deadlocked 2-2 on a proposed $2.25 million contract renewal with Flock Safety for 290 ALPR cameras, effectively blocking the expansion. Opponents cited Flock's data-sharing with federal agencies including ICE, a new lawsuit alleging OPD illegally shared ALPR data with federal authorities, and the city's Privacy Advisory Commission's refusal to endorse the plan.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Councilmembers Carroll Fife and Rowena Brown voted against a police plan to approve a $2.25 million contract with Flock Safety.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock has violated contracts with other sanctuary cities by sharing data with the federal government for immigration enforcement and lying about it",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    },
    {
      "quote": "a former member of the Privacy Advisory Commission sued the department for allegedly breaking state and local law by repeatedly sharing its ALPR data with federal authorities",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
